27 Jul 2022 : the core loop of the mandelbrot has been rewritten
              to use the fma calls. This may be verified on various
              systems with : 

                objdump -D -Mpower4 -j .text xmand > xmand.dis


24 Jul 2022 : see document readme.data for the data dump format

08 Jul 2022 : any attempt to use FMA on some old hardware throws SIGILL

08 Jul 2022 : thus far I do see two different results from the
              dataset1 

    input parameters 32768 268435456 0.399750960350502282381 0.205251797480741515756 4 

    two results based on fast with FMA or not 

        9b010ac9db3dd2be89317fcb1aa635f6e4963a6f981f4741e9e23a1062003bbf
        e4348e24b0bcedde099f07203037a5063504af9b98fda5612128fd823cfd1c3c

    An old Pentium II 400MHz machine from 1998 agrees with the second
    result above as does a 32-bit armv7l based linux machine.

    The dataset2 parameters result in reasonable results also :

    input parameters 32768 274877906944 -0.0157887752805699992098 +1.02061921088799989477 4 

    results from old Pentium II :

        0185154e797afdf219199d2922ed6d20bf9877a0f46a3ab6a19ba996985bfbb1


29 Jun 2022 : when in doubt do a disasseble to check for FMA opcodes

                objdump -D -Mintel -j .text xmand > xmand.dis



24 Mar 2022 : currently focused on a single dataset in order to 
              get repeatable data into timestamp files named with
              a timestamp. Date to be used to test and verify the
              code written for future NVidia CUDA enabled GPUs.

